# NSG fix: zero-counter KPM reports (PRB/UL read 0 while traffic flows)
#
# Reference note (distro trees are the source of truth; build-slim.sh bakes
# them). One file pair changes:
#   src/mmwave/model/mmwave-enb-net-device.{h,cc}
#
# ── Symptom ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Whole runs where RRU.PrbUsedDl and DRB.PdcpSduBitRateUl read exactly 0 while
# DRB.UEThpDl shows healthy throughput. Deterministic per binary (buildings
# runs hit it reliably, plain baselines intermittently) — any rebuild shifted
# which runs were affected, which made it look haunted.
#
# ── Root cause: two builder chains resetting one set of counters ─────────────
# Instrumentation caught the smoking gun:
#   [NSG-DU] t=0.200232  sym=1  denom=0  winNs=232141
# The GUI/file-logging builders (BuildGUIDu/CuUp/CuCp) self-reschedule every
# 100 ms and RESET THE SAME windowed KPM counters the E2 report reads
# (ResetPhyTracesForRntiCellId etc.). So every E2 report window was clipped to
# <=100 ms; and when the E2 build landed microseconds after a GUI build, the
# window was shorter than one slot — the PRB denominator
#   ceil(window_ns / slot_ns) * 14
# uses INTEGER division, hits 0, and the guarded division leaves macPrb = 0
# for every UE. UL PDCP counters likewise sampled freshly-reset. Cumulative
# RLC-based throughput still read fine, hence the contradictory-looking
# "thp > 0 with PRB = 0" reports. Which report the xApp captured depended on
# wall-clock sim speed — hence per-binary determinism.
#
# ── Fix (two layers) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. The GUI/file-logging chains now run ONLY in offline file-logging mode
#    (m_forceE2FileLogging) — in E2 mode nothing consumes their csv output and
#    they have no business resetting live KPM windows.
# 2. Guard in BuildAndSendReportMessage: if a build lands < 10 ms after the
#    previous one, skip it (log "[NSG] ... skipped a zero-window E2 report
#    build") and just reschedule — an all-zero report can never be emitted.
#
# ── Verified (2026-07-17) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Baseline x3: PRB 7.9-9.1, UL 368-439 kbps (previously 0.0 on this binary);
# buildings: PRB 4.0 with SINR 24.9 / DL 8.93. Full fidelity harness 9/9
# "ALL LEVERS WIRED" — including the "L4 PRB consistency" guard that first
# caught this. NOTE: PRB values are now computed over the true 0.5 s windows
# (earlier "healthy" runs were measured over GUI-clipped <=100 ms windows, so
# absolute PRB levels shifted slightly; the levers all still move correctly).
